      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can some of this accumulation be done in 16-bit?\nGiven that the input is uint8_t, each symmetric pair sum is at most 510, and the filter is fixed to `{ 56, 12, -3, -1 }`. So the -3, -1, and +12 taps should fit safely in int16_t; only the +56 tap needs to widen to int32_t.\n\nAlso, since one filter value is known to be -1, that tap could just be a vector subtract instead of a multiply.",
