      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T10:16:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we use running src/dst pointers here instead of keeping both data/outrow state? The input side already behaves like a row cursor, and dst could follow the same pattern:\n\n    const uint8_t *src \u003d \u0026intbuf[j];\n    uint8_t *dst \u003d \u0026output[j];\n\n    ...\n    vst1_u8(dst, res);\n    dst +\u003d out_stride;\n\nThis would avoid recomputing dst_col + outrow * out_stride and make the sliding-window pointer movement a bit easier to follow.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 892,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 894,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "3b164d8a4d65960befd1dbc15c7bfd373652f496",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
